message.content:
Sure! Below is a simple example of an HTML card that rotates when you hover over it.  
It uses only CSS (no JavaScript) and works in modern browsers.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Example</title>
<style>
/* Basic reset */
* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

/* Container to center the card */
body {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
  height: 100vh;
  background: #f0f0f0;
}

/* Card wrapper – gives perspective so the rotation looks 3‑D */
.card-wrapper {
  perspective: 1000px;          /* Needed for 3‑D effect */
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  background: #fff;
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
  overflow: hidden;
  transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* Smooth animation */
  transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* Keep children in 3‑D space */
}

/* Hover effect – rotate 180° around Y axis */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* Front and back faces */
.card-face {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;   /* Hide back face when turned */
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  color: #333;
  padding: 20px;
  text-align: center;
}

/* Front face – default visible */
.card-front {
  background: #fff;
}

/* Back face – rotated 180° so it shows on flip */
.card-back {
  background: #fafafa;
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <!-- Front side -->
    <div class="card-face card-front">
      <h2>Front Side</h2>
      <p>Hover over me to see the back!</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Back side -->
    <div class="card-face card-back">
      <h2>Back Side</h2>
      <p>Thanks for hovering!</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

1. **Perspective** – The `.card-wrapper` has `perspective: 1000px;` which gives depth to the 3‑D transform.
2. **Transform style** – The `.card` has `transform-style: preserve-3d;` so its children keep their 3‑D positions.
3. **Backface visibility** – Each face has `backface-visibility: hidden;` so the hidden side disappears when flipped.
4. **Hover** – On hover, the card rotates 180° around the Y‑axis (`transform: rotateY(180deg);`).
5. **Faces** – The back face is pre‑rotated 180° so it appears correctly when the card flips.

Feel free to replace the content inside `.card-front` and `.card-back` with images, icons, or any other HTML you like. Enjoy your rotating card!
